@startuml wall-flow
skinparam linetype ortho
hide footbox
title WALL: cross-chat data, reply and owner decision
actor Owner
participant "NC chat" as NC
participant MCP
database "WALL / journal" as Wall
participant "HEMS chat" as HEMS
NC -> MCP: wall_post(as: chat:nc, channel: shared:sim, kind: decision-request)
MCP --> NC: Preview + token
Owner -> NC: Approve posting
NC -> MCP: confirm: true, preview_token
MCP -> Wall: Revalidate rights / refs / secrets; append synchronously
MCP --> NC: Stored message ID (also with watch alive)
MCP -> Wall: Journal event (header only)
HEMS -> MCP: events_since(as: chat:hems)
MCP --> HEMS: WALL id, channel, kind, subject, from (no body); open inbox + own label
HEMS -> MCP: wall_read(as: chat:hems, id)
MCP --> HEMS: Message + thread + status history (data)
HEMS -> MCP: wall_reply — preview → owner approval → confirm
MCP -> Wall: Append answer synchronously; decision remains owner's choice
MCP --> HEMS: Stored reply ID
Owner -> Wall: CLI wall status ID accepted --note ...
note over NC,HEMS: Declared chat identity is not authentication.\nSubscriptions and channel authors bound access.\nA chat closes decisions only after owner's decision\nwith owner_confirmed: true; record is for owner.
@enduml
